1
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Behind-the-Scenes Cast Interview)

2
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:06,390
(Li Bangbang as Bu Kakao)
Hello, everyone.

3
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,830
I'm rapper, Li Bangbang.

4
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:10,050
This is your first time on The Truth.

5
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:11,570
How does it feel to be an NPC?

6
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:13,230
My first time as an NPC on The Truth

7
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:15,510
feels really interesting.

8
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,630
(A new experience)
It's very fun.

9
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:18,630
I get to work

10
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:20,430
(Door of Truth Animal World)
with so many actors

11
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:21,910
in these wonderful costumes.

12
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,190
It was really fun.

13
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,250
When you first met
the cast of The Truth,

14
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:26,780
what were your first impressions?

15
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,590
My impression of them really

16
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,430
went up.

17
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:32,150
I think even more highly of them now.

18
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:32,750
I only

19
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:34,470
used to see on them TV.

20
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:36,830
(Breaking through the screen)
Meeting them in real life

21
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:39,790
and not seeing them
through a screen makes them

22
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:42,710
(Nothing but praise)
even prettier and more handsome.

23
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:44,470
Who left the strongest impression
on you?

24
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,830
Liu Yuning left the strongest impression

25
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:49,150
on me.

26
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:49,790
Why is that?

27
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,910
Well, you don't often

28
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:53,750
come across actors

29
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,430
that are that tall.

30
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:57,270
So when I saw him...

31
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:58,670
You know when you see someone

32
00:00:58,680 --> 00:00:59,470
really tall,

33
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,830
there's this sense

34
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:03,230
of pressure you don't normally feel.

35
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:04,630
I look at him.

36
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:05,670
He's so tall and handsome,

37
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:06,670
and sings well too.

38
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:08,430
(Impressive)
He's impressive.

39
00:01:08,430 --> 00:01:10,470
It's your first time playing an NPC
in a mystery show,

40
00:01:10,470 --> 00:01:13,570
so it's quite a big challenge for you.

41
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:15,220
How did you feel

42
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:16,240
about the experience?

43
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:19,670
I'd say I gained a lot from it.

44
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,990
Because throughout the process,

45
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:22,870
normally,

46
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,750
we might play these games
in our free time.

47
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:27,310
But seeing things
from an NPC's perspective

48
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:28,430
to guide others

49
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:30,630
to uncover the truth step by step

50
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:32,750
(Another rewarding day)
feels totally different.

51
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:35,460
Did anything interesting happen

52
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:36,820
while you were acting
with the players today?

53
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:40,150
I was supposed to save everyone

54
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:42,670
and help them leave safely.

55
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,150
So I got pretty close to everyone

56
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:46,150
because I was playing a dog.

57
00:01:46,160 --> 00:01:47,110
So I went

58
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:49,230
and stood beside them.

59
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,470
But they all wanted to push me away.

60
00:01:51,480 --> 00:01:52,590
They suspected me.

61
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:54,190
How should I put it?

62
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:57,190
I felt a little flustered.

63
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,590
(Didn't expect that to happen)
But I still saw it through to the end

64
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,070
and covered their escape.

65
00:02:01,410 --> 00:02:03,590
If you had another chance,
what role would you like to play?

66
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:06,150
I really like to play

67
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:08,350
(Push yourself)
a really vicious character.

68
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,870
I'm usually pretty cheerful.

69
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:12,950
Always laughing and joking around.

70
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,150
I've never really had the chance

71
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:16,230
to play a more ruthless character

72
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:18,470
in a murder mystery.

73
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,710
Everyone knows

74
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:21,950
the villains are quite ruthless.

75
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:23,670
So I hope I'll get the chance.

76
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:25,870
(I'll show you what I'm made of)
I can show everyone

77
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,790
what I can do.

78
00:02:26,790 --> 00:02:28,990
Do you usually
enjoy playing escape rooms?

79
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:30,910
I love them.

80
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,510
When I'm in Tianjin,

81
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,230
we'll get a group to play together.

82
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:35,990
But I'm get scared easily.

83
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,790
I actually have some experience.

84
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:39,950
When I'm in Tianjin,

85
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:42,030
I often help my friends out
by playing NPCs.

86
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,470
When you watch from the outside,

87
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:45,150
or when you're playing,

88
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:45,990
you think those people

89
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,510
who scare you are terrifying.

90
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,510
When you're in a pitch-black room,

91
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,990
hearing the scary music
while scaring people,

92
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,190
you get scared yourself.

93
00:02:54,200 --> 00:02:55,150
So I'm really grateful.

94
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:57,550
I got this chance to experience things

95
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:59,070
from another perspective.

96
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:02,070
That I could be an NPC

97
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,230
and help bring the story to life.

98
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,150
I'm really glad.

99
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:07,680
If you had to recommend this episode
to the viewers,

100
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:08,390
what would you say?

101
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:10,270
It'll be that one line.

102
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:11,590
Crack the case with The Truth.

103
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,150
Big budget savings with Tongcheng.

104
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:14,430
When the truth is uncovered,

105
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:17,030
we set out with Tongcheng.

106
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,190
(Tai Wei as Tai Kule)
Hello, everyone.

107
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,950
I am actor, Tai Wei.

108
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,390
I'm glad to meet everyone

109
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,150
on The Truth.

110
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:25,430
Today, I play the character, Tai Kule.

111
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:27,390
When you first met
the cast of The Truth,

112
00:03:27,390 --> 00:03:28,960
what were your first impressions?

113
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,590
Beautiful.

114
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,870
It's my first time here,

115
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:35,790
and I get to play such
an important role.

116
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:39,390
I had a great time with all the players.

117
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:42,400
So, going from a comedian
to playing an NPC on a variety show,

118
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,710
what would you say is
the biggest difference?

119
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:46,310
I think the difference from comedy

120
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:48,710
is having to improvise
and react on the spot.

121
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:49,630
I think

122
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,670
even though you know your part

123
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,190
of the script,

124
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,430
you also have

125
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:56,550
to take in whatever the guests tell you

126
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:57,670
and use that information

127
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,030
to give the guests

128
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:01,790
what they need to know.

129
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,030
(Give them guidance)
So it's challenging

130
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:04,990
to improvise.

131
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,670
During this shoot,

132
00:04:06,670 --> 00:04:08,470
was there anything
particularly memorable?

133
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:12,070
Jin Jing called me Tarzan.

134
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:12,990
(Laughs)
I clearly

135
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,590
have a bear right here.

136
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,310
Still called me Tarzan.

137
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:17,610
Which player's reaction

138
00:04:17,610 --> 00:04:18,990
left the biggest impression on you?

139
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:21,510
I think...

140
00:04:21,520 --> 00:04:25,950
the boys were very brave.

141
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:27,070
When I opened the door

142
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,390
to rescue them,

143
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:29,990
I remember

144
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,590
no one really lost control.

145
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:35,590
But Zhang Ruonan was

146
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,870
just completely

147
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,350
out of it. Yeah.

148
00:04:39,350 --> 00:04:42,230
What new character or gameplay
would you like to try next time?

149
00:04:43,160 --> 00:04:47,230
Next time, I'd like...

150
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:50,550
(Supervillain)
I can be the baddest villain around.

151
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:53,270
If you had to recommend this episode
to the viewers,

152
00:04:53,270 --> 00:04:54,160
what would you say?

153
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,910
The case if full of twists.

154
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,590
The NPC performances are fantastic.

155
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:05,230
(Completely lost in the maze)
Players are baffled.

156
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:07,990
So it's fun to watch.

157
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:09,670
(Fu Jiahua as Gorilla)
Hello, everyone.

158
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,430
I am actor, Fu Jiahua.

159
00:05:11,580 --> 00:05:12,960
Of all the episodes you've filmed,

160
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,800
what scene left
the biggest impression on you?

161
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,550
The scene that left
the biggest impression...

162
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,950
There are so many.

163
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:20,110
If I had to pick one,

164
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,270
I'd say the one we just did

165
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:23,270
is quite impressive.

166
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:26,150
The whole scene was so immersive,

167
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:27,630
and there was...

168
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:29,070
I was like a...

169
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,470
Because when I watched movies,

170
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:32,350
I really love those kinds of scenes.

171
00:05:32,360 --> 00:05:33,550
(Rally the troops)
A pre-battle rally.

172
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:35,710
Someone standing up there

173
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,310
waving their arms.

174
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:37,990
When everyone
has lost their will to fight,

175
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:38,830
someone steps up and says,

176
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:39,550
"We can't give up."

177
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:40,430
"We have to fight!"

178
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:41,150
And so on.

179
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:43,350
Suddenly, everyone is fired up.

180
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,430
The scene we just did

181
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,110
was a little like that.

182
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:49,150
So it stuck with me.

183
00:05:49,150 --> 00:05:50,500
During the whole ceremony,

184
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:53,260
what kind of player reaction
made you feel most accomplished?

185
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:55,310
I'm not sure if it's considered
a sense of accomplishment.

186
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,470
But I think

187
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,430
when I was talking

188
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,110
about taking revenge,

189
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,950
the players were also discussing
among themselves.

190
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:02,310
Whenever I look at them,

191
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:03,190
they'd meet my eyes

192
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,950
and will...

193
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:06,470
do this.

194
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:08,030
Like they were caught talking in class

195
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,390
by their teacher.

196
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:10,550
Of course, they were also

197
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:13,030
playing along with my character.

198
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,430
But in that moment,

199
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:16,550
they gave me a boost too.

200
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:19,550
(The fire of revenge)
When they kept chanting "revenge".

201
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:21,390
It made me believe

202
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:23,470
even more in the scene and my character.

203
00:06:23,470 --> 00:06:26,850
Which player's interaction today
almost made you laugh?

204
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,830
I was holding back my laughter

205
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,390
with every player.

206
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,430
Because they are...

207
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,430
When they saw me,

208
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:35,270
they'd act like

209
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:36,710
(Old acquaintance)
they're tired of me.

210
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:37,790
So I was just...

211
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:38,590
But thankfully,

212
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:39,710
everyone was very professional.

213
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:41,110
We immediately got immersed again

214
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:42,990
and went back

215
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,830
to acting like we'd never met.

216
00:06:44,840 --> 00:06:45,750
Yeah. And today...

217
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:47,070
I don't know if they'll air this,

218
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,310
but when I making my rounds...

219
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:50,070
Because before this,

220
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:52,190
I've never done

221
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,990
a scene with so many people.

222
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:57,270
When the players

223
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:58,030
entered the scene,

224
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,430
the place was packed.

225
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,990
There was a point
I couldn't get through.

226
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,990
So while reciting the ceremony lines,

227
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,590
I had to tell Zhang Ruonan

228
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:06,390
(Nowhere to stand)
to let me pass.

229
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:06,790
Thank you.

230
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,430
I'm sorry.

231
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:08,230
It's alright.

232
00:07:08,230 --> 00:07:10,080
You played the Gorilla this time.

233
00:07:10,490 --> 00:07:12,130
What was the most memorable moment?

234
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:14,870
The most memorable part

235
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,430
was how hard I tried
to portray a gorilla.

236
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,990
I watched a lot

237
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,390
of movies about gorillas
turning into humans

238
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:21,470
like "Rise of the Planet of the Apes"

239
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:22,550
and the behind-the-scenes.

240
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:23,190
The actors

241
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,950
would use props

242
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,870
to mimic how gorillas move.

243
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:29,670
When a gorilla gets angry,

244
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:30,190
it does this.

245
00:07:30,190 --> 00:07:31,720
(Did some serious research)

246
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,470
They'd do this.

247
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:33,630
Then they eat,

248
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:35,550
they even purse their lips.

249
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:37,070
Using their lips to grab the food first.

250
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:37,910
They don't eat like humans.

251
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,390
We bite with our teeth first.

252
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,710
Gorillas start with their lips.

253
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,430
Like this.

254
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:43,390
So I did a ton of research

255
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,550
on how to play a gorilla.

256
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:45,270
But then...

257
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:46,510
Then they told me

258
00:07:46,520 --> 00:07:47,990
after I got injection in the scene,

259
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,470
I have to act like a human.

260
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:50,430
So I spent all that time practicing

261
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,870
in my room,

262
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:52,830
only to be told I had to act human.

263
00:07:54,690 --> 00:07:55,350
What new character

264
00:07:55,350 --> 00:07:57,360
or gameplay would you like
to try next time?

265
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:58,750
If it's possible,

266
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:01,310
let's try an episode

267
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:03,950
set in the NPC universe.

268
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,390
They push the door

269
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:06,310
and see me. Close it.

270
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:06,830
Opens another.

271
00:08:06,840 --> 00:08:07,630
I've changed costumes,

272
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:08,350
but I'm still there.

273
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,350
They open another,

274
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,390
and I'm there too.

275
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:12,510
So I'm everywhere.

276
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,830
Yeah. But that's a little hard
to pull off.

277
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,150
But I honestly

278
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,630
haven't really though about

279
00:08:17,640 --> 00:08:18,910
what kind of character

280
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:21,670
to play in The Truth.

281
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,310
I'll just see what roles need me.

282
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:25,230
I will do my best

283
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:28,070
to bring it to life

284
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:30,670
as close as possible
to what everyone envisions.

285
00:08:31,010 --> 00:08:32,210
If you had to recommend this episode

286
00:08:32,210 --> 00:08:33,500
to the viewers in one sentence,

287
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:34,140
what would you say?

288
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:38,620
Insanely handsome, insanely gorgeous,
insanely good, insanely funny!

289
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:39,940
(Wu Ni as Lamb)

290
00:08:39,940 --> 00:08:40,290
(Fang Yuan as Dalmatian)

291
00:08:40,290 --> 00:08:40,640
(Xiao Yuting as Cow)

292
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:41,030
(Lin Ke'ai as Squirrel)

293
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:41,380
(Xu Zeyan as Lion)

294
00:08:41,380 --> 00:08:44,520
Did you prepare different lines
or reactions

295
00:08:44,520 --> 00:08:45,740
for different players?

296
00:08:46,390 --> 00:08:48,350
During the testing,

297
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:50,870
some players might

298
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:52,910
interact with us

299
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:55,430
or try to find clues

300
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:57,830
from us.

301
00:08:57,840 --> 00:09:00,470
They would try to figure out

302
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,790
what made us different.

303
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,990
So they'd hope

304
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,430
or needed to find out

305
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,710
the difference between humans
and animals.

306
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:08,670
So they'd come talk to us.

307
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,350
Since we were playing animals,

308
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:12,510
if they failed to prove themselves,

309
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,430
we'd naturally suspect
that they were humans

310
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,510
or something else.

311
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:16,990
So we'd respond accordingly.

312
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:18,880
Any funny moments

313
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:20,490
when interacting with the players?

314
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,350
I think the funniest part

315
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:24,830
was when we were leaving.

316
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,550
Our gorilla host

317
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:28,510
ask the players

318
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:29,950
if they were humans.

319
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,550
One of them

320
00:09:31,560 --> 00:09:33,910
pointed at one of us

321
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:36,390
who looked particularly human and asked,

322
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:37,070
"Are you human?"

323
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:37,510
Yes.

324
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:38,470
I thought

325
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,430
that was hilarious.

326
00:09:40,430 --> 00:09:43,840
Which player impressed you the most?

327
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,430
They all left quite an impression.

328
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:48,350
(Everyone's handsome and beautiful)
they're all incredibly gorgeous.

329
00:09:48,360 --> 00:09:50,150
I couldn't look away.

330
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:51,350
We had a great time together.

331
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,910
I think Zhou Keyu.

332
00:09:52,920 --> 00:09:53,910
When he first came in,

333
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:54,830
he gave us

334
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,150
an animal performance.

335
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,310
It was pretty novel.

336
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:59,350
He basically charged in.

337
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:01,030
Since we were

338
00:10:01,040 --> 00:10:02,230
playing animals,

339
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:04,430
they players entered

340
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,190
and tried to blend in with us,

341
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,990
adding their own performance.

342
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,150
They were great.

343
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:11,750
How did you feel about playing an NPC

344
00:10:11,750 --> 00:10:12,450
on The Truth?

345
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:13,190
Did you do any preparation?

346
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:16,110
Of course I did.

347
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:16,590
First of all,

348
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:19,110
I was thrilled to work
with so many talented people.

349
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:21,630
Each of us played

350
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,350
a different character.

351
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,830
I would prepare in advance.

352
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:27,070
You can see I'm playing a lion.

353
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:29,270
I'd watch films about lions

354
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:30,230
and how to portray them

355
00:10:30,240 --> 00:10:31,590
to practice,

356
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,870
so I could flesh out the character

357
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:35,230
and fit in with everyone.

358
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:37,230
I play a dog

359
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:38,430
and have a dog at home.

360
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,830
When I played with my dog at home,

361
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,870
so I...

362
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:43,990
Although I'm human,

363
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,750
my body language needed

364
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:47,670
to have that playful puppy quality

365
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:48,750
or other mannerisms.

366
00:10:48,760 --> 00:10:50,830
I'd study all of that carefully.

367
00:10:50,830 --> 00:10:52,200
Did any player's performance

368
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,800
strike you as particularly funny?

369
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:54,950
Zhou Keyu.

370
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:56,230
It's Mr. Zhou.

371
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:58,710
I also thought Jin Jing's acting

372
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:01,310
was really memorable.

373
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:03,150
She actually wanted

374
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:05,390
to explore the place

375
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,390
and find out
what ceremony we were doing,

376
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:10,550
or figure out what other interactions
she could have.

377
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:11,830
She wanted to fit in with us.

378
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:13,990
She used her own approach

379
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,070
and her acting to blend in.

380
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:16,710
Yeah.

381
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,070
During the assessment

382
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,630
to see if she was an animal

383
00:11:19,640 --> 00:11:20,350
or a human,

384
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:21,470
she did a little dance

385
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:23,390
on the other side of the screen.

386
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:25,070
it was pretty cute and playful.

387
00:11:25,070 --> 00:11:25,500
Yeah.

388
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:26,510
That stood out to me.

389
00:11:28,170 --> 00:11:30,690
(Yang Huaizu as Doberman)
How do you feel playing an NPC

390
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:31,420
on The Truth.

391
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:32,340
Did you do any preparation?

392
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,110
Well.

393
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:35,630
When we were rehearsing on set,

394
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:37,990
we were completely immersed

395
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,190
in the atmosphere of the ritual.

396
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:43,990
The... atmosphere

397
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,510
made me feel rather heavy,

398
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,110
but I was completely absorbed.

399
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:51,350
During the actual shoot,

400
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:53,030
we became even more immersed.

401
00:11:53,040 --> 00:11:54,590
So I think when you

402
00:11:54,600 --> 00:11:56,150
put your whole heart

403
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:57,670
into doing something,

404
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:59,990
that's what left
the deepest impression on me.

405
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:03,580
Was there a player's animal acting
that left a deep impression on you?

406
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,790
It would be Jin Jing's.

407
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,830
Because toward the end, she...

408
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:10,670
(Jin so funny)
was a little funny, you know?

409
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:12,270
Just seeing her

410
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:13,870
and the faces she made.

411
00:12:13,880 --> 00:12:14,910
Based on that,

412
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,550
I found her really funny.

413
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:19,310
At the end,

414
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:22,110
when we looked in the mirror,

415
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,590
that really stuck with me too.

416
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:25,920
(Runrun as Tui Haowan)

417
00:12:25,930 --> 00:12:27,040
As the director of the NPCs,

418
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,980
what was it like
playing an NPC yourself?

419
00:12:29,470 --> 00:12:30,250
Well.

420
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:31,510
As a director,

421
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:33,070
you guide the players

422
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,310
through the content

423
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,390
and the story

424
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:38,110
from the perspective of an observer.

425
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:40,270
You sort of know everything.

426
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:40,750
But when you

427
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,070
actually play

428
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:42,790
an NPC yourself,

429
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,510
you realize

430
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:46,590
it takes a very strong sense
of conviction.

431
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,230
You really have
to immerse yourself in it.

432
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:50,750
So it's quite challenging.

433
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:51,910
(Same scene, different experience)
So that's a pretty

434
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:53,750
new experience for me.

435
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:55,050
After these few shoots,

436
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:56,860
what moment left
the deepest impression on you?

437
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,390
Not exactly a moment.

438
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,270
I think

439
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,870
it was getting to work
with all the players

440
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:04,710
because they're all very dedicated,

441
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:05,990
(Praise the cast)
highly professional,

442
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,030
and incredibly cooperative.

443
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:10,070
I worked with Wu Bi,

444
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,630
Cui Shaoyang,

445
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:12,590
He Wenjun,

446
00:13:12,600 --> 00:13:13,670
Li Yi,

447
00:13:13,680 --> 00:13:14,990
Sun Leyan,

448
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,390
and Li Fei.

449
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:18,550
Getting to know them in real life

450
00:13:18,560 --> 00:13:20,030
is completely different

451
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,710
from seeing them onscreen.

452
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:22,230
In person,

453
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:23,750
they're all very down to earth,

454
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:25,590
extremely cooperative,

455
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,270
and very professional.

456
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:28,070
Basically, once you explain the scene,

457
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:28,830
just once,

458
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:30,550
they immediately understand

459
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:33,070
and can deliver exactly

460
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:33,830
what we have in mind.

461
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:35,270
They'll even add their own twist

462
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,510
to make the character

463
00:13:36,520 --> 00:13:38,030
feel more complete.

464
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:39,830
(Everyone builds on it together)
So I hope everyone watching

465
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:41,270
will keep an eye out

466
00:13:41,280 --> 00:13:43,910
for their work

467
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:45,350
and continue to support them.

468
00:13:45,350 --> 00:13:47,890
If you had to recommend this episode
to the viewers in one sentence,

469
00:13:47,890 --> 00:13:48,400
what would you say?

470
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,630
Please.

471
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:51,190
I'm begging everyone.

472
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:53,950
So many of us on this production

473
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:55,990
give it everything we've got

474
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,110
to bring you the best content we can.

475
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,590
Give it a watch. You won't regret it.

476
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:02,710
Whether you have criticism or praise,

477
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:04,310
we're ready to take it all.

478
00:14:06,340 --> 00:14:07,260
=The Truth (Season 4)=

479
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:08,430
